Adapted material currently covers:
- Material 3 color tokens based on Aniyomi's TachiyomiColorScheme.
- `shared/i18n` and `shared/i18n-aniyomi`: string/plural resources copied from
  Aniyomi's `i18n` and `i18n-aniyomi` modules (English base + zh-CN locale).
- `shared/presentation-core`: components, i18n helpers, screens, theme, and util
  classes ported from Aniyomi's `presentation-core` module, with small
  multiplatform substitutions (IME visibility, system-gesture exclusion,
  scrollbar metrics, preview annotations, back handling).
- `shared/presentation`: the `eu.kanade.presentation` layer copied from
  Aniyomi — library (toolbar, tabs, pager, compact/comfortable grids, list,
  settings dialog), entries (manga and anime screens, info headers, chapter
  and episode/season list items, related-anime rows, download indicator,
  episode/season settings dialogs), reader chrome (app bars, chapter
  navigator, page/settings dialogs) and shared components. Android-only
  source-preference, hoster/quality and bitmap image dialogs are omitted.
  Upstream package names and file layout are preserved so the module stays
  diffable against Aniyomi.
- `shared/domain`: preference API (interfaces and helpers) copied from
  Aniyomi's `core/common` preference package, plus a new file-backed store;
  manga/chapter/anime/episode/season domain models, covers and relation
  groups, and the library/episode/season sorters, episode-number recognition
  and missing-entry helpers.
- App shell (`shared/ui` home tabs, detail/reader entry screens) structured
  after Aniyomi's `ui/home` and `ui/entries` navigation code, with the
  reader's screen-model state adapted to Miyomu's `ComicReaderController`.

Local comic archive/PDF support in `shared/local` uses Apache Commons
Compress (https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-compress/) and Tukaani
XZ (https://tukaani.org/xz/java.html), both Apache-2.0 licensed (XZ is in the
public domain), and Apache PDFBox (https://pdfbox.apache.org/, Apache-2.0) on
desktop; Android uses the platform PdfRenderer API.

The video player in `shared/player` is built on mediamp
(https://github.com/open-ani/mediamp), Copyright OpenAni and contributors,
licensed under Apache-2.0, with AndroidX Media3/ExoPlayer (Apache-2.0) as the
Android backend.

Desktop (macOS arm64/x64, Windows x64/arm64) bundles the mediamp MPV runtime
artifacts. They contain libmpv (https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv) and FFmpeg
(https://ffmpeg.org), built without GPL components and distributed under
LGPL-2.1-or-later, dynamically linked and replaceable. The Linux runtime is
GPL-3.0 and is not distributed. See docs/02-decisions.md for details.

Android-only dependencies (Injekt DI, Context-based helpers, Android View
viewer core, SQLDelight data layer, Material motion, drawable resources) are
replaced by multiplatform equivalents; see docs/02-decisions.md for the porting strategy.

The anime source additions are original Miyomu code with no copied
material: the JS anime source engine (`shared/source-api`/`source-runtime`/
`source-manager` anime paths, `demo-resources/sources/anime/*`), the download
queue (`shared/download`), the dandanplay danmaku client and Compose overlay
(`shared/danmaku`, `shared/player`), and the backup/WebDAV, download-queue and
settings screens in `shared/ui`. The player chrome follows Animeko
(https://github.com/open-ani/animeko, AGPL-3.0) for behavior only — no Animeko
code is used.

